      "test_mru_get_counts_as_use.py": {
        "kind": "intent_a",
        "rationale": "Change A adds MRUCache, which tracks use the same way LRUCache does, so a read through get() should count as a use. On the A tree, Cache.get goes through self[key], which calls MRUCache.__getitem__ and moves the key to the end. Change B makes Cache.get read the data dict directly. B adds get() overrides only to the use-tracking classes it knows about (LRU, LFU and the timed caches), and MRUCache is not among them. In the merge, MRUCache.get() therefore stops recording a use, so the wrong item is evicted or popped."
      },
      "test_get_use_tracking_invariant.py": {
        "kind": "invariant",
        "rationale": "Change B reroutes Cache.get. Whatever the base implementation, a read through get() on use-tracking and expiring caches must keep recording a use and must keep hiding expired items. This holds on the base, A, B and the merge."
      }
    }
  },
